    "own_line": true,
    "norm": "Tests {@link Symmetry010Date#range(TemporalField)}, i.e. the valid value range that a given temporal field can take for a specific Symmetry010 date. <p> In the Symmetry010 calendar, 2012 is a common (364-day) year and 2015 is a leap (371-day) year whose December holds an extra \"leap week\", which is why the leap-year cases below report wider day/week ranges."
   },
